opennyai_summary.decision:
6. Considering the facts and circumstances of these case and also keeping in mind the principle of parity, it is just and proper to allow these appeals.
Hence, I proceed to pass the following:-
NC: 2024:KHC:41261 ORDER Criminal Appeal No. 1758/2024 and Criminal Appeal No.1759/2024 are allowed.
The order dated 17.09.2024 passed in Criminal Misc. No.560/2024 and Criminal Misc.No.559/2024 by the Court of Principal District and Sessions Judge, Mandya are set aside subject to following conditions:
Diwakar Avasti (A-3) vs State Of Karnataka on 9 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/183686788/
3 a.
Appellant/accused Nos.2 and 7 shall surrender before the I.O/Jurisdictional Court within a period of 10 days from the date of receipt of this order;
b. They are directed to be released in the event of their arrest/surrender as noted above, in Crime No.241/2016 and Crime No.258/2015 of Mandya West Police Station;
c.
They shall execute a personal bond for sum of Rs.2,00,000/- each with two sureties for the likesum;
NC: 2024:KHC:41261 d.
They shall be available for the purpose of investigation as and when necessary and co- operate with the investigation of the case; e.
They shall not tamper with the prosecution witnesses/evidence and shall not cause any threat or inducement to the complainants/victims;
f. They shall furnish proof of their residential address/mobile numbers and inform the I.O/Court, if there is change in the address or mobile numbers;
g. They shall not leave the country without prior permission of the learned Sessions Judge; h. They shall appear before the Jurisdictional Court regularly.

